        "Content": "\n23/10/2026 - 12:00\n\nFOR SALE BY LIVE STREAM PROPERTY AUCTION, FRIDAY 23RD OCTOBER AT 12.00 NOON.\n\nYou Must Pre-Register on Our Website by Thursday 22nd to bid.\n\nO'Donnellan & Joyce are delighted to offer for sale by auction this 3-bedroom mid-terrace property in Mervue, presenting an exciting opportunity for anyone looking for a full renovation project in a well-established Galway location.\n\n12 Barry Avenue has been vacant for a number of years and is now in need of a complete refurbishment. The property offers buyers the chance to take on a project and transform the existing house into a modern home tailored to their own requirements. With the right vision and investment, there is plenty of scope to unlock the potential of this property.\n\nThere may also be grant assistance available for refurbishment works, subject to the relevant criteria and approvals.\n\nThe accommodation currently comprises an entrance hall, living room, bathroom, kitchen/dining room and laundry room on the ground floor. Upstairs, there are three bedrooms.\n\n While the property requires significant upgrading, the existing layout provides a good starting point for a comprehensive renovation.\n\nThe location is another major attraction. Mervue is a popular and well-connected part of Galway, with Mervue Primary School, Radharc na Mara National School and Galway Community College all close by. ATU's Creative Arts and Media campus on Wellpark Road is also within easy reach.\n\nThere are excellent employment and commercial facilities nearby, including Liosbán and Mervue Industrial Estate, while Galway's major healthcare and medtech employers are also located close by, including Merlin Park Hospital, Bon Secours Private Hospital, Galway Clinic, Boston Scientific, Merit Medical and Creganna.\n\nFor commuters, the M6 and M18 motorway networks are easily accessible, providing good connections to Galway, Dublin, Limerick and beyond.\n\nFor buyers looking for a property with potential, 12 Barry Avenue offers the chance to take a dated and vacant house and create something of their own. Whether approached as a renovation project, future family home or investment opportunity, this property is well worth considering.\nViewing is highly recommended for anyone looking for a project in a convenient Galway location.\n\nSOLICITOR WITH CARRIAGE OF SALE: Mr. Karl O'Connor, 2nd Floor, 16 Merchants Road, Galway, H91T3CP.\n\nAUCTION PROCESS \n\nPre-Registration Required in Order to Bid By Phone or Online. Please familiarize yourself with the Auction Process prior to bidding.\n\nPlease note the following:\n\n5,000 bidder security fee must be paid in advance to bid on the day (if unsuccessful this is fully refunded to you) If you are successful, you are immediately contracted on the drop of the hammer and the non-refundable balance of 10% must be paid immediately. \n\nPhone and Online bidding service available you must pre-register to bid prior to Auction Day - you can register on our website under the auction tab at top of the homepage. \n\n\nRegister for legals on our website under the auction tab at top of the homepage (please note all legals may not be available for download until closer to the auction date - once you have registered you will receive an alert when they do become available). We always advise potential purchasers to have their solicitor review legals prior to bidding.\n\n\nNOTE: These particulars are not to be considered a formal offer. They are for information only and give a general idea of the property. They are not to be taken as forming any part of a resulting contract, nor to be relied upon as statements or representations of fact. \n\nFLOORPLANS: The floor plan including furniture, fixture measurements and dimensions are approximate and for illustrative purposes only. The Polycam App used gives no guarantee, warranty or representation as to the accuracy and layout. All enquiries must be directed to the agent.\n\nWhilst every care is taken in their preparation, neither O'Donnellan & Joyce Auctioneers nor the vendor accept any liability as to their accuracy. Intending purchasers must satisfy themselves by personal inspection or otherwise as to the correctness of these particulars.\n\nNo person in the employment of O'Donnellan & Joyce Auctioneers has any authority to make or give any representation or warranty whatever in relation to this property. \n\nNote: Prospective purchasers must satisfy themselves as to the condition and suitability of the property, its existing or potential use, any development or redevelopment potential, any necessary planning permissions or other consents, and as to the availability of and eligibility of the property and/or any prospective purchaser for any grants, schemes or funding. No representation or warranty is made or given by or on behalf of the Vendor in relation to any such matters."
      },
